2. BOUNDARY VALUE ANALYSIS ->
                  - it focuses on testing the boundary of valid  and invalid input ranges 
            application-> can cast vote - 18-70
                - Developers cna often make mistakes as 
                    1. using"<" instead of "<="
                    2. using ">" instead of ">=" 
        - in such cases using the equivalance partitioning may not reaveal the defects 
    BOUNDARY VALUE ANALYSIS (BVA)
                        - below minumun (17)
                        - just minimum (18) 
                        - above mminimum (19)
                        - below maximun (69)
